   "file": "content/FMA_22830/tier1.md",
   "text": "The semispinalis capitis muscles on both sides work together to tilt the head back. But when only one of these muscles works, the head tilts and turns toward that muscle's side. Each semispinalis capitis runs from the spine to the occipital bone at the back of the skull.",
